 | `Rule30GateTrap`, `Rule30Certificates.GateTrap` | 2026-10-31 | A trap for the gate of the period-2 sideways reduction: `u R`, column 1 at the odd times of a right half `R` driven by the alternating column. A set of 829 sixteen-cell windows is closed under the double step whatever the cells further right do, and inside it, after a black cell of column 1, the next one comes 3 or 5 double steps later. So for every right half whose window enters it the black cells of `u R` come from then on with gaps 3 or 5. The empty right half enters it at time 293, so after its black cell at step 146 `u ∅` is a concatenation of `001` and `00001`, its gate `r ↦ u ∅ (146 + r)` satisfies `Rule30DrivenPrefix.Window` and `Rule30SpacingRenormalization.Spaced`, and its transform is not spaced. `Q01Gap` (**open**): no finitely supported constrained start of the zero-boundary left half has free bits whose complement, from some step on, has each black cell followed by the next one 3 or 5 steps later. `Q01` implies it, and it gives `¬ FinSupp (Psi R)` for every right half whose window enters the trap, hence `CQ01Empty`. The windows and the six kernel checks are in `Rule30Certificates.GateTrap`. Contributed by Renaud Bosdure as Rule 30 Prize submission [`R30-20261027-230bc7`](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261027-230bc7). AI used: Claude (Anthropic), Gemini (Google) and Grok (xAI). | `gaps_of_entry`, `u_empty_gaps`, `u_empty_window`, `emptyGate_window`, `u_empty_spaced`, `u_empty_transform_not_spaced`, `Q01Gap_of_Q01`, `not_finSupp_Psi_of_Q01Gap`, `CQ01Empty_of_Q01Gap` |
